AGENTS.md	- Runtime environment variables use the `NATIVE_SHELL_` prefix for the shell itself and `NATIVE_CMD_` for the bundled command layer. `NATIVE_SHELL_BIN` names the running shell binary (the `bash`/`sh` faces resolve it to this installation's real `native-shell.exe`), `NATIVE_SHELL_INVOKED_AS` carries the shim-forwarded invocation face, and `NATIVE_CMD_PATH` selects one exact command-layer dispatcher executable (file or directory) for the session. During the transition, native-shell also sets/reads the deprecated `WINUXCMD_PATH` and `WINUXCMD_HOME` names because current rubash upstream still reads them; these bridges are marked with comments and must be removed once rubash renames its readers. Native Shell also sets/reads the deprecated `WINUXSH_SHELL` and `WINUXSH_ROOT` names because current rubash upstream still reads them; these bridges are marked with comments and must be removed once rubash renames its readers. (The `*_SHELL_PATH_STYLE` pair was retired rubash-side in rubash#556 / rubash#537: the engine always renders `$PWD`/`pwd` in the POSIX persona form, and native-shell no longer exports the variables.)
AGENTS.md	- Use `~/.native-shellrc` as the primary-only interactive user entry point for plugin lists, theme selection, exports, aliases, functions, and shell startup logic. Do not read, migrate, delete, or modify the legacy `~/.winuxshrc` and `~/.winshrc` startup files. An explicitly opted-in `~/.bashrc` fallback is a future plan only, not supported behavior. Startup must not automatically run setup or plugin sync, create the primary rc, or rewrite user rc files. Issue #359 case A (1.4.2): plugin management never writes the rc at all — the manifest (`plugins.toml` + `sources/registry.toml`) drives the generated loader `~/.native-shell/generated/plugins.nsh`, which the host sources read-only BEFORE the user rc; `native-shell setup` still writes the rc (create/whole-file) until its 1.4.3 create-only convergence. Never re-attach the retired managed-block writers (`assets::write_managed_block`/`remove_managed_block`) to any verb — the 359.12 structure ratchet fails the build's test suite if you do.
