scripts/release/rubash-pin.json	    "Pinned to JayWanX/rubash 0c955b4a - 'Send the invocation face under the current variable name'. The shim forwarded the bash/sh invocation face under the legacy NIU_INVOKED_AS name while Native Shell reads NATIVE_SHELL_INVOKED_AS, so `bash --help` printed the product help and failed the staged-release face gate, and `bash -c 'echo $0'` printed native-shell instead of bash.",
scripts/release/rubash-pin.json	    "The same fork carries e84ffd77 - 'Find the host shell by its current name, not the pre-rename one' - which rewires the shim's locate_shell() away from the legacy niu.exe/winuxsh.exe names and onto native-shell.exe. Without both commits a staged <root>/cmd/usr/bin/bash.exe neither finds the shell (exit 127) nor reproduces the GNU face.",
scripts/release/rubash-pin.json	  "description": "Rubash source pin for native-shell releases (rubash#827, conclusion B). Every release job fetches exactly this rubash commit into ../rubash -- where the [patch] path override in Cargo.toml deterministically picks it up -- and fails the release unless the checked-out HEAD equals rubash_rev. The compiled engine is pinned to an exact commit instead of being 'whatever rubash main HEAD was at build time'. The engine now comes from JayWanX/rubash (our fork): upstream unixwin/rubash still ships the pre-rename bash shim lookup chain (the legacy niu.exe / winuxsh.exe names), which cannot find native-shell.exe and exits 127.",
